From: erosqcfw <erosqcfw@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tag/Pool: shrink the tag pool hash table to 4096 buckets

The static 16384-bucket table is 128 kB of .bss; with a ~4k-song
database every page of it is dirtied (measured 132 kB resident on
EROS Q). 4096 buckets (32 kB) keep the average chain ~1.3 long.

---
--- a/src/tag/Pool.cxx	2026-10-03 21:34:12.666396774 +0000
+++ b/src/tag/Pool.cxx	2026-10-03 21:34:12.685774708 +0000
@@ -77,7 +77,11 @@
 				       value);
 }
 
-static IntrusiveHashSet<TagPoolItem, 16384,
+/* erosq: 16384 buckets x 8 B = 128 kB of .bss that a ~4k-song library dirties
+   completely (every page gets an entry). 4096 buckets = 32 kB keeps chains
+   short (~1.3 entries per bucket at ~5k unique tag values) and saves ~96 kB of
+   resident anonymous memory on a 32 MB device. */
+static IntrusiveHashSet<TagPoolItem, 4096,
 	IntrusiveHashSetOperators<TagPoolItem, TagPoolItem::GetKey,
 				  TagPoolKey::Hash,
 				  std::equal_to<TagPoolKey>>,
